    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4499264": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty Applied Behavior Analysis",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty Applied Behavior Analysis. Assumption University. Description The Master’s degree program in Applied Behavior Analysis at Assumption University in Worcester, MA is seeking an adjunct faculty member to teach a course on measurement and research methods in applied behavior analysis for the Spring 2027 semester. Graduate classes meet once per week on campus in the late afternoon or evening. The semester runs from January 19 through May 6, 2027. For more information about the ABA programs at Assumption University, visit https://www.assumption.edu/graduate/applied-behavior-analysis Application Instructions: To apply, please submit (1) a letter of interest, (2) a current curriculum vitae, and (3) the names and contact information for two references who can attest to the applicant’s teaching experience and qualifications. Finalists will also be asked to provide official transcripts of academic work. Materials should be submitted as MS Word documents. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Sitting, standing, walking, and bending are required of this position. Use of a computer keyboard and computer screen for periods of time with close vision and the ability to adjust visual focus plus manual dexterity are required. MENTAL DEMANDS: The mental demands described are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Examples of mental demands include reading (documents), detailed work, confidentiality, language, math, reasoning, oral communications, written communications, customer contact, multiple concurrent tasks, constant interruptions, and performing calculations when necessary. About Assumption University: St. John Paul II wrote: “Man’s creation by God ‘in his own image’ confers upon every human person an eminent dignity; it also postulates the fundamental equality of all human beings.” Assumption University recognizes the essential contribution of a diverse community of students, staff, and faculty and condemns all forms of harassment, discrimination, and disrespect. As such, and in compliance with the requirements of federal law and/or the laws of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts, Assumption University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, disability, age, veteran status, marital status, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, and pregnancy, as well as other legally protected status, in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities, except where such conditions may constitute bona fide qualifications for the programs or activities in question. Requirements Applicants should have an MA/MS or PhD (preferred) in applied behavior analysis or a related field and possess the BCBA or BCBA-D credential. Preference will be given to candidates with graduate-level teaching experience. Applicants must be willing to contribute actively to the mission of the University as well as show respect for the Catholic and Assumptionist identity of Assumption University."
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4365171": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty of Psychology",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty of Psychology. Assumption University. Description The Psychology Department at Assumption University in Worcester, MA seeks to hire an instructor to teach one section of PSY 253: Psychology of Learning during the Spring 2027 semester. The semester runs from January 19 to May 10 (inclusive of finals period). Adjunct instructors are welcome members of the department, and are provided with office space, email, voicemail, and support and resources needed for quality teaching. Successful candidates may have the possibility of teaching additional courses in subsequent semesters. For more information about the Psychology Department, visit: https://www.assumption.edu/undergraduate/psychology To apply, please submit a (1) letter of interest, (2) current curriculum vitae, and (3) the names and contact information for two references who can attest to the applicant's teaching experience and qualifications. In the cover letter, we invite candidates to describe their experiences working with a diverse student body. Finalists will also be asked to provide official transcripts of academic work. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Please direct any inquiries to Dr. Leamarie Gordon, department chairperson, at lt.gordon@assumption.edu. PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Sitting, standing, walking, and bending are required of this position. Use of a computer keyboard and computer screen for periods of time with close vision and the ability to adjust visual focus plus manual dexterity are required. MENTAL DEMANDS: The mental demands described are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Examples of mental demands include reading (documents), detailed work, confidentiality, language, math, reasoning, oral communications, written communications, customer contact, multiple concurrent tasks, constant interruptions, and performing calculations when necessary. About Assumption University: St. John Paul II wrote: “Man’s creation by God ‘in his own image’ confers upon every human person an eminent dignity; it also postulates the fundamental equality of all human beings.” Assumption University recognizes the essential contribution of a diverse community of students, staff, and faculty and condemns all forms of harassment, discrimination, and disrespect. As such, and in compliance with the requirements of federal law and/or the laws of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts, Assumption University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, disability, age, veteran status, marital status, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, and pregnancy, as well as other legally protected status, in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities, except where such conditions may constitute bona fide qualifications for the programs or activities in question. Requirements Applicants with a PhD in Behavior Analysis or Psychology are preferred. ABD doctoral candidates will also be considered. Individuals with a terminal master's degree in behavior analysis or psychology with experience teaching at the college level will also be considered. In addition to being part of the Major in Psychology, the Psychology of Learning course is the foundational course in Assumption’s Minor in Applied Behavior Analysis. Applicants should be prepared to teach topics related to behaviorism, Pavlovian learning, and operant learning."
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4258486": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty in Biology",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty in Biology. Assumption University. Description The Department of Biological and Physical Sciences at Assumption University seeks to hire two to three part-time adjunct instructors for the fall 2026 semester. The department needs to staff one section of BIO390 Exercise Physiology, one section of BIO390L Exercise Physiology Lab, and one-two sections of BIO150L Principles of Biology Lab. Exercise Physiology is an upper-level biology course that is taken by students pursuing a concentration in Pre-Physical Therapy and some students majoring in biology. Principles of Biology Lab is the introductory biology lab course for new nursing students. Class meetings run from August 31 to December 16, which includes the final exam week. Adjuncts are welcomed as important contributors to the department, to our students, and are provided with office space, email, voicemail, support for using our learning management system (Brightspace), and other resources needed for quality teaching. Successful candidates may have the possibility of teaching additional courses in subsequent semesters. Application Instructions: Please submit a letter of interest, current curriculum vita, and the names and contact information for two references who can attest to the applicant's teaching experience and qualifications. In the cover letter, we invite candidates to describe their experiences working with a diverse student body. Finalists will also be asked to provide official transcripts of academic work from the highest degree-granting institution and two written letters of recommendation. Materials must be submitted online as MS Word documents or PDF files at the following website: www.assumption.edu/hr. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position(s) is filled. Appointments are contingent on course enrollments. PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Sitting, standing, walking, and bending are required of this position. Use of a computer keyboard and computer screen for periods of time with close vision and the ability to adjust visual focus plus manual dexterity are required. MENTAL DEMANDS : The mental demands described are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Examples of mental demands include reading (documents), detailed work, confidentiality, language, math, reasoning, oral communications, written communications, customer contact, multiple concurrent tasks, constant interruptions, and performing calculations when necessary. ABOUT ASSUMPTION UNIVERSITY: St. John Paul II wrote: “Man’s creation by God ‘in his own image’ confers upon every human person an eminent dignity; it also postulates the fundamental equality of all human beings.” Assumption University recognizes the essential contribution of a diverse community of students, staff, and faculty and condemns all forms of harassment, discrimination, and disrespect. As such, and in compliance with the requirements of federal law and/or the laws of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts, Assumption University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, disability, age, veteran status, marital status, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, and pregnancy, as well as other legally protected status, in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities, except where such conditions may constitute bona fide qualifications for the programs or activities in question. Requirements Applicants must be willing to contribute actively to the mission of the University as well as show respect for the Catholic and Assumptionist identity of Assumption University. Applicants should have a PhD in Biology or DPT for candidates applying to teach Exercise Physiology. ABD graduate students with prior teaching experience will also be considered."
