    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4611401": {
      "title": "Tenure - Track Assistant Professor of Theology",
      "description": "Tenure - Track Assistant Professor of Theology. Assumption University. Description The Department of Theology at Assumption University (Worcester, MA) invites applications for a full-time tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor. Applicants should be demonstrably conversant with the entirety of the Catholic theological tradition and its reception in the patristic, medieval, modern, and contemporary periods. Individuals with specialization in the application of Catholic anthropology to questions of bioethics and medical practice are especially encouraged to apply. Candidates must be committed to undergraduate teaching and advising as well as service to the theology department, the university, and the greater community. The ideal candidate would teach introductory and advanced courses in the University’s major and minor programs in theology and in the University’s core curriculum program. The candidate will also have the opportunity to teach courses within their area of expertise. Candidates must also be able to provide evidence of scholarship and promise of developing a research program. As a Theology Department at a Catholic institution, a successful candidate is encouraged to seek the mandatum from the bishop. For more information about the Theology Department, visit: https://www.assumption.edu/undergraduate/theology Application Instructions: To apply please submit: A letter of application Current curriculum vita Statement of teaching philosophy Research statement Samples of representative research papers, Transcripts from any colleges or universities attended. In the cover letter, we invite candidates to describe their experiences working with a diverse student body. Candidates should provide names and contact information for three references who can attest to the applicant's teaching and research experience and qualifications. We will begin review of materials in earnest by late November 2026. PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Sitting, standing, walking, and bending are required of this position. Use of a computer keyboard and computer screen for periods of time with close vision and the ability to adjust visual focus plus manual dexterity are required. MENTAL DEMANDS: The mental demands described are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Examples of mental demands include reading (documents), detailed work, confidentiality, language, math, reasoning, oral communications, written communications, customer contact, multiple concurrent tasks, constant interruptions, and performing calculations when necessary. About Assumption University: St. John Paul II wrote: “Man’s creation by God ‘in his own image’ confers upon every human person an eminent dignity; it also postulates the fundamental equality of all human beings.” Assumption University recognizes the essential contribution of a diverse community of students, staff, and faculty and condemns all forms of harassment, discrimination, and disrespect. As such, and in compliance with the requirements of federal law and/or the laws of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts, Assumption University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, disability, age, veteran status, marital status, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, and pregnancy, as well as other legally protected status, in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities, except where such conditions may constitute bona fide qualifications for the programs or activities in question. Requirements Doctorate in theology by the date of hire; Experience teaching at the college level Candidates should actively contribute to the mission of the University and its Catholic and Assumptionist identity"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4603315": {
      "title": "Clinical Coordinator PA Program",
      "description": "Clinical Coordinator PA Program. Assumption University. Description Full-time 12-month Professor of Practice in the PA Program and School of Health Professions. Responsibilities include working with the Director of Clinical Education to assist with management of the clinical phase of the program, in addition to teaching and other duties as assigned. The Clinical Coordinator will collaborate with the Program Director and Associate Program Director in the organization, administration, continuous and periodic review and assessment, planning, development, and general effectiveness of the program and the curriculum. The Clinical Coordinator will also collaborate with program leadership and the faculty in development, review, and revision of the mission statement, program vision, and program goals. PRINCIPAL ACCOUNTABILITIES: Assists the Director of Clinical Education with management of the clinical phase of the program, including, but not limited to, the following duties: Maintain and update clinical affiliation agreements Maintain and update all preceptor information, including license and board certification information Clinical rotation scheduling Correspondence and other communication with preceptors and clinical site staff Send and track evaluations Complete clinical site visits Procure and maintain clinical sites Track student hours, patient encounter logs, student absences, and reported incidents Review and grading of SOAP notes Acts as advisor to matriculated PA students for both the didactic and clinical years to include documented counseling and mentoring sessions. Participates in all Program and university processes deemed necessary by the Program and Associate Program Directors, including service on faculty committees. Assists in the review of applications for admission to include conducting interviews and supporting the recruitment and selection of students. OTHER DUTIES: Supports the Director of Admissions, Assessment, and Academic Success in the development and implementation of remedial instruction and assessment tools. Assists in development, review, and revision of the PA Program mission, vision, goals, and competencies. Assists the Associate Program Director in the organization, administration, continuous and periodic review, planning, development, and evaluation of the effectiveness of the PA Program. Teaches courses with which he/she has demonstrated competence and/or experience and as assigned by the Program Director. Participates in lab, small group, and simulation activities. Participates in University events as a representative of the PA Program and the School of Health Professions. Participates in events external to the Program that increase awareness and reputation of the PA Program. Assists the Associate Program Director with the preparation and analysis for ARC-PA accreditation activities and reports. Participates in the interviewing process and selection of faculty members at the request of the Program Director. Regularly attends all scheduled staff and faculty meetings. PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Sitting, standing, walking, and bending are required of this position. Use of a computer keyboard and computer screen for periods of time with close vision and the ability to adjust visual focus plus manual dexterity are required. MENTAL DEMANDS: The mental demands described are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Examples of mental demands include reading (documents), detailed work, confidentiality, language, math, reasoning, oral communications, written communications, customer contact, multiple concurrent tasks, constant interruptions, and performing calculations when necessary. About Assumption University: St. John Paul II wrote: “Man’s creation by God ‘in his own image’ confers upon every human person an eminent dignity; it also postulates the fundamental equality of all human beings.” Assumption University recognizes the essential contribution of a diverse community of students, staff, and faculty and condemns all forms of harassment, discrimination, and disrespect. As such, and in compliance with the requirements of federal law and/or the laws of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts, Assumption University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, disability, age, veteran status, marital status, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, and pregnancy, as well as other legally protected status, in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities, except where such conditions may constitute bona fide qualifications for the programs or activities in question. Requirements Must possess and maintain NCCPA certification Must maintain an active state license to practice as a physician assistant Must have a Master’s Degree in a health-related discipline Must have a minimum of 5 years of experience as a practicing PA Must be willing to contribute actively to the mission of the University, as well as show respect for the Catholic and Assumptionist identity of Assumption University PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Greater than 5 years of clinical experience Greater than 3 years of teaching experience, preferably in higher education Experience teaching in a PA program or medical school Experience with ARC-PA accreditation"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4597954": {
      "title": "Tenure - Track Assistant Professor in Education",
      "description": "Tenure - Track Assistant Professor in Education. Assumption University. Description Assumption University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track assistant professor position in the Education Department specializing in Secondary English Education and/or Multilingual Learners beginning Fall 2027. The successful candidate will maintain an active research and publication record; teach in-person courses; conduct field-based supervision; develop and maintain collaborative partnerships with local schools; and fulfill advising and other duties as needed by the Education Department and University. Application Instructions: Please submit 1) Cover letter 2) Current Curriculum Vitae 3) Teaching Statement 4) Names and contact information for three references who can attest to the applicant's teaching experience and qualifications Materials must be submitted online as MS Word documents or PDF files The deadline for application materials is November 29, 2026. PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Sitting, standing, walking, and bending are required of this position. Use of a computer keyboard and computer screen for periods of time with close vision and the ability to adjust visual focus plus manual dexterity are required. MENTAL DEMANDS: The mental demands described are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Examples of mental demands include reading (documents), detailed work, confidentiality, language, math, reasoning, oral communications, written communications, customer contact, multiple concurrent tasks, constant interruptions, and performing calculations when necessary. About Assumption University: St. John Paul II wrote: “Man’s creation by God ‘in his own image’ confers upon every human person an eminent dignity; it also postulates the fundamental equality of all human beings.” Assumption University recognizes the essential contribution of a diverse community of students, staff, and faculty and condemns all forms of harassment, discrimination, and disrespect. As such, and in compliance with the requirements of federal law and/or the laws of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts, Assumption University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, disability, age, veteran status, marital status, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, and pregnancy, as well as other legally protected status, in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities, except where such conditions may constitute bona fide qualifications for the programs or activities in question. Requirements Ph.D./Ed.D. in Language, Literacy, Curriculum and Instruction, Bilingual Education, Secondary English Education, or a related field. Demonstrated expertise in literacy development (grades 5-12) and language acquisition, drawing on evidence-based practices. Familiarity with the Massachusetts English Language Arts and Literacy Curriculum Framework. Experience mentoring and supervising teachers and/or teacher candidates. Commitment to working as part of a collaborative team Willingness to contribute actively to the mission of the University as well as showing respect for the Catholic and Assumptionist identity of Assumption University. Desired Qualifications: K-12 teaching license in secondary English (5-12), ESL, or related field. Massachusetts Sheltered English Immersion (SEI) Endorsement Three or more years of teaching experience as a classroom teacher. Experience teaching in a teacher preparation program Experience with K-12 partnerships Experience teaching courses in curriculum and methods in secondary English, adolescent literacy development, teaching multilingual learners, reading and writing across the curriculum, introductory education courses, related graduate-level courses, and field supervision"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4597867": {
      "title": "Tenure- Track Assistant Professor in Early Literacy Education",
      "description": "Tenure- Track Assistant Professor in Early Literacy Education. Assumption University. Description Assumption University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track assistant professor position in the Education Department specializing in Language, Literacy, and Multilingual Learners beginning Fall 2027. The successful candidate will maintain an active research and publication record; teach in-person courses; conduct field-based supervision; develop and maintain collaborative partnerships with local schools; and fulfill advising and other duties as needed by the Education Department and University. Application Instructions: Please submit: 1) Cover letter 2) Current Curriculum Vitae 3) Teaching Statement 4) Names and contact information for three references who can attest to the applicant's teaching experience and qualifications Materials must be submitted online as MS Word documents or PDF files The deadline for application materials is December 1, 2026. PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Sitting, standing, walking, and bending are required of this position. Use of a computer keyboard and computer screen for periods of time with close vision and the ability to adjust visual focus plus manual dexterity are required. MENTAL DEMANDS: The mental demands described are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Examples of mental demands include reading (documents), detailed work, confidentiality, language, math, reasoning, oral communications, written communications, customer contact, multiple concurrent tasks, constant interruptions, and performing calculations when necessary. About Assumption University: St. John Paul II wrote: “Man’s creation by God ‘in his own image’ confers upon every human person an eminent dignity; it also postulates the fundamental equality of all human beings.” Assumption University recognizes the essential contribution of a diverse community of students, staff, and faculty and condemns all forms of harassment, discrimination, and disrespect. As such, and in compliance with the requirements of federal law and/or the laws of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts, Assumption University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, disability, age, veteran status, marital status, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, and pregnancy, as well as other legally protected status, in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities, except where such conditions may constitute bona fide qualifications for the programs or activities in question. Requirements Ph.D./Ed.D. in Language Development, Literacy Education, Reading Education, Curriculum and Instruction, Bilingual Education, or a related field. Demonstrated content area expertise in early literacy (grades K-3), literacy development (grades 4-6) and language acquisition, drawing on evidence-based practices. Familiarity with the Massachusetts English Language Arts and Literacy Curriculum Framework. Experience mentoring and supervising teachers and/or teacher candidates Commitment to working as part of a collaborative team Willingness to contribute actively to the mission of the University as well as showing respect for the Catholic and Assumptionist identity of Assumption University. Desired Qualifications: K-12 teaching license in reading/literacy, elementary education, or related field. Massachusetts Sheltered English Immersion (SEI) Endorsement Three or more years of teaching experience as a classroom teacher or reading specialist. Experience teaching in a teacher preparation program Experience with K-12 partnerships and grants Experience teaching courses in early literacy development, teaching multilingual learners, children’s literature, introductory education courses, related graduate-level courses, and field supervision."
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4599128": {
      "title": "Tenure - Track Assistant Professor in Criminology",
      "description": "Tenure - Track Assistant Professor in Criminology. Assumption University. Description The Sociology and Criminology Department at Assumption University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Criminology to start in Fall 2027. This position will help support our sociology and criminology program and share responsibility primarily for the criminology program curriculum with existing faculty. This includes teaching the two introductory courses, Introduction to the Criminal Justice System and Criminology, and upper-level electives in the new faculty’s area of expertise. Preference will be given to candidates with quantitative research expertise or experience teaching undergraduate or graduate social science Statistics courses. Areas of expertise are open. While not required, the ideal candidate will also have some familiarity with the field of Sociology and the ability to teach introductory sociology or sociology elective courses as department needs arise. Application Instructions: Please submit: Cover letter that includes an overview of teaching and scholarly interests and progress, Current curriculum vita Names and contact information for three references who can attest to the applicant's teaching experience and qualifications. Short-listed applicants will be asked to submit writing samples, evidence of teaching effectiveness, research statement, and copies of unofficial or official transcripts, Materials must be submitted online as MS Word documents or PDF files To receive consideration for the position, applications must be received by December 1, 2026 . PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Sitting, standing, walking, and bending are required of this position. Use of a computer keyboard and computer screen for periods of time with close vision and the ability to adjust visual focus plus manual dexterity are required. MENTAL DEMANDS: The mental demands described are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Examples of mental demands include reading (documents), detailed work, confidentiality, language, math, reasoning, oral communications, written communications, customer contact, multiple concurrent tasks, constant interruptions, and performing calculations when necessary. About Assumption University: St. John Paul II wrote: “Man’s creation by God ‘in his own image’ confers upon every human person an eminent dignity; it also postulates the fundamental equality of all human beings.” Assumption University recognizes the essential contribution of a diverse community of students, staff, and faculty and condemns all forms of harassment, discrimination, and disrespect. As such, and in compliance with the requirements of federal law and/or the laws of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts, Assumption University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, disability, age, veteran status, marital status, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, and pregnancy, as well as other legally protected status, in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities, except where such conditions may constitute bona fide qualifications for the programs or activities in question. Requirements Applicants should have a PhD in Criminology, Criminal Justice, Sociology (with a demonstrated concentration in Criminal Justice and/or Criminology),or closely related academic field. ABD graduate students with prior teaching experience will also be considered. Applicants must be willing to contribute actively to the mission of the University as well as show respect for the Catholic and Assumptionist identity of Assumption University."
    }
